# Suricata IDS Integration with Splunk for Network Threat Detection and SOC Monitoring

## 1. Abstract

This project demonstrates the implementation of a network security monitoring environment using Suricata Intrusion Detection System (IDS) integrated with Splunk. Suricata was configured to inspect network traffic and generate security events and alerts. The generated logs were collected and forwarded to Splunk, where they were indexed, searched, analyzed, visualized, and used for security alerting.

A dedicated Suricata index and SOC monitoring dashboard were created in Splunk. The dashboard provides visibility into Suricata event types, alert activity over time, source IP addresses, destination IP addresses, and recent security alerts. A scheduled Splunk alert was also configured to identify Suricata detection events.

The project demonstrates a basic Security Operations Center (SOC) workflow involving log collection, security event analysis, detection, visualization, and alerting.

---

## 2. Introduction

Modern networks generate large amounts of security-related data. Intrusion Detection Systems can identify suspicious network activity, but security analysts need centralized monitoring and analysis to investigate these events effectively.

Suricata is an open-source, high-performance IDS/IPS and network security monitoring engine. Splunk is a security information and event management and data analysis platform that can collect, index, search, and visualize security logs.

In this project, Suricata was integrated with Splunk to create a centralized network threat monitoring environment. Suricata generated network security events, while Splunk was used to analyze the events and provide a SOC-style monitoring dashboard and detection alerts.

