## 6. Suricata Configuration

Suricata was installed and configured in the Kali Linux environment.

The Suricata service was verified using:

```bash
sudo systemctl status suricata
```

The primary event log used in the project was:

```text
/var/log/suricata/eve.json
```

The log contains structured security events generated by Suricata.

Custom detection rules were configured in:

```text
/etc/suricata/rules/local.rules
```

The custom rules were used to detect ICMP-related network activity during testing.

---

## 7. Splunk Integration

The Splunk Universal Forwarder was configured to collect Suricata event logs and forward them to the Splunk server.

The forwarding connection was verified using:

```bash
/opt/splunkforwarder/bin/splunk list forward-server
```

The connection was confirmed as active.

Suricata events were stored in a dedicated Splunk index:

```spl
index=Suricata
```

The successful appearance of Suricata events in Splunk confirmed that the log forwarding and ingestion process was working.

---

## 8. Detection and SPL Queries

Splunk Search Processing Language (SPL) was used to analyze the Suricata events.

### View Suricata Events

```spl
index=Suricata
```

### View Suricata Alerts

```spl
index=Suricata event_type=alert
```

### Suricata Event Types

```spl
index=Suricata
| stats count by event_type
| sort - count
```

### Alerts Over Time

```spl
index=Suricata event_type=alert
| timechart count
```

### Top Source IP Addresses

```spl
index=Suricata event_type=alert
| stats count by src_ip
| sort - count
| head 10
```

### Top Destination IP Addresses

```spl
index=Suricata event_type=alert
| stats count by dest_ip
| sort - count
| head 10
```

### Recent Suricata Alerts

```spl
index=Suricata event_type=alert
| table _time src_ip src_port dest_ip dest_port proto alert.signature
| sort - _time
```

